answer:
For steady-state diffusion through a slab,

\[
J=P_M\frac{\Delta p}{\ell}
\]

Given \(P_M=2.2\times10^{-13}\ \frac{(\mathrm{cm^3\,STP})(\mathrm{cm})}{\mathrm{cm^2\cdot s\cdot Pa}}\)

\[
\Delta p=(2000-150)\ \mathrm{kPa}=1850\ \mathrm{kPa}=1.85\times10^6\ \mathrm{Pa}
\]

\[
\ell=15\ \mathrm{mm}=1.5\ \mathrm{cm}
\]

Thus,

\[
J=(2.2\times10^{-13})\frac{1.85\times10^6}{1.5}
\approx 2.7\times10^{-7}
\]

\[
\boxed{2.7 \times 10^{-7}}
\]
